WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.700
Step three lints the program's definition.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.425
With a one-hour timeout: no findings.

3
00:00:05.425 --> 00:00:10.455
With a fifteen-minute timeout, L X eleven
finds that the worst-case retry waits,

4
00:00:10.455 --> 00:00:12.499
nine hundred and sixty seconds,

5
00:00:12.499 --> 00:00:15.800
reach the callback timeout,
and the exit code is two.

6
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.512
So the retries have to
fit inside the wait.

7
00:00:18.512 --> 00:00:23.437
Step four runs the program's
definition for GCC High, three ways.

8
00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:27.055
Through two transient failures:
three downstream calls,

9
00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:29.363
one effect, and the task is completed.

10
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:32.648
Through five failures:
five calls, no effect,

11
00:00:32.648 --> 00:00:36.663
and the task is failed, at once,
not at the end of the wait.

12
00:00:36.663 --> 00:00:39.462
And with two deliveries
of the same request:

13
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:42.650
two calls, but one effect,
and the task is completed.

14
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.313
The idempotency key means
the work is done once.

15
00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:52.075
Every callback goes to the
GCC High Graph host, on v1.0.

16
00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:55.200
The slide joins each run's last two lines.
